{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem","id":595782,"title":"No tutor, no problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-19T11:28:01-07:00","id":595782,"title":"No tutor, no problem","content":"So I'm starting up a campaign which may include new players. As such I don't want to toss them into the deep end of vampric politics. So I have an idea for a less social and more personal campaign, but I'm trying to come up with a good initial justification for it. Essentially I want to have a group of players who are turned then dumped by the wayside without learning so much that sun bathing is a really bad idea. I had an idea about a group of anarchistic vampires trying to swell the ranks of unaligned vampires to undermine the Covenants through sheer numbers. But that still doesn't square to why they wouldn't stick around to tutor them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:15:58-07:00","id":595840,"title":"","content":"They could be Sabat-style shovelheads, embraced and buried just to be cannon fodder for a raid on an Invictus-controlled city or something. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could all be survivors of the same use of the Mass Embrace Scale. Maybe their shared sire didn't get out of the blood pit fast enough and they killed him/her in their Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:16:40-07:00","id":595842,"title":"","content":"Pethaps, rather than being abandoned, their sire(s) embraced them and was planning on filling them in on all they needed to know as per usual but instead disappears (dead or staked, who knows), leaving them with no knowledge of their condition. To give them a bit of an ear in perhaps their sire has a ghoul, who doesn't know much but can provide them with some very basic information, provided they keep him/her fed.<br /> <br /> Later on they could investigate what happened to their sire and learn about his membership in this anarchistic group. You could then start introducing the covenants as the guys who probably took him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:20:24-07:00","id":595845,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Strix killed them all, gathered them in one place, and then used a unique dread power to raise them all at once as it ran away to watch the results from a distance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:28:10-07:00","id":595848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem?p=595840#post595840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could be Sabat-style shovelheads, embraced and buried just to be cannon fodder for a raid on an Invictus-controlled city or something.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could all be survivors of the same use of the Mass Embrace Scale. Maybe their shared sire didn't get out of the blood pit fast enough and they killed him/her in their Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good ideas all around from everyone. At least I have something to think on and it doesn't feel too out of place. To give more information, the basic idea I had before the embrace was the players for some reason or another attending the Burning Man Festival. They wake up the following night after the festival ends to what should be some form of hangover, only to feel very peculiar. Then leave the players to pick up the pieces and discover themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:33:23-07:00","id":595852,"title":"","content":"Tough not entirely by the rules in Requiem, you could have an accidental Embrace: they're exanguinated somehow and them fed blood before death's final call. An accident in a factory, some people mangled and bleeding, but still living, a desperate vampire or even ghoul where there with the Vitae needed in bags and started to feed them so they could survive. Maybe some of them where in fact turned into ghouls that way, but the PCs just had bled too much and became Kindred instead.<br /> <br /> Maybe they're the last shot of a previous coterie. Their sires embraced them before an attack, those older vampires where killed or forced to flee and leave the PCs alone.<br /> <br /> Or you could pretty well finish things with the Frenzy explanation. The newly Embraced too oftem frenzy during the process. Sometimes the sire to be just isn't prepared to such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T13:02:37-07:00","id":595878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem?p=595848#post595848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good ideas all around from everyone. At least I have something to think on and it doesn't feel too out of place. To give more information, the basic idea I had before the embrace was the players for some reason or another attending the Burning Man Festival. They wake up the following night after the festival ends to what should be some form of hangover, only to feel very peculiar. Then leave the players to pick up the pieces and discover themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok, so not quite as violent as where my mind went with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, how about this - they weren't intentionally embraced. They were just snacks for a vampire or group of vampires who were at Burning Man, but for some strange reason they <i>all</i> rose as Revenants. When the game starts, the festival is over, and all of the PCs are full vampires, and have the Amnesia Condition. How did they get from Revenants to Vampires? Did they find vampires to uplift them? Are they all unwitting diablerists? Or did something much stranger happen? They'll have to piece it together to find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T13:33:32-07:00","id":595930,"title":"","content":"One of the quieter motives behind putting revenants in the 2e core was to provide a way for groups to be Embraced. Your characters could have all been fed on by vampires, then &quot;died&quot; on the way home in a car accident or something. The revenant rules are a bit punishing to hit an entire coterie with at once, but you could just borrow the metaphysics and start the player characters as regular neonates.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full\" target=\"_blank\">first edition demo</a> also provides a justification for a diverse coterie of newly Embraced vampires, and in general works as a crash course in the setting for new characters and players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:02:06-07:00","id":595951,"title":"","content":"Okay, so an idea that I will need to flesh out. It borrows ideas from both the Malkavian disease and VII. It involves a secret covenant that is slowly spreading beneath the notice of Kindred society. It swells its ranks by means of a ritual that creates bonded coteries. The members of these coteries are amnesiac. They are left to their own devices by their sires. This may seem callous, but another effect of the ritual that is part of their embrace creates a subconscious mental web connecting the members like a twisted pyramid scheme. The neonates have flashes or dreams that urge them to the bidding of their sires. The stronger and older the members grow, and the more initiates they put beneath them, the stronger their connection and control over this psychic web grows.<br /> <br /> When members of this covenant come across &quot;proper&quot; vampires, their beast reacts in an alien way. It creates an inherent bubbling feeling of xenophobia that makes blending in with one of the major Covenants difficult. (though there are a few secret agents who manage to do just that).<br /> <br /> Only the eldest members know the end game. Swell the numbers, then rise up and replace the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:27:59-07:00","id":596209,"title":"","content":"Hm, that all sounds a lot stupider now that I typed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T21:05:50-07:00","id":596480,"title":"","content":"One of the first Vampire games I played in was a Masquerade story called the &quot;Dunk-Tank&quot; chronicle: Several people were embraced by sires of different clans, and woke up in an underground bunker, stocked with blood bags, but with no other clues as to what had happened. The game broke up before we met our sires. (so far as we knew)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T22:15:53-07:00","id":596500,"title":"","content":"I don't think it sounds stupid, that would depend entirely upon the story you write. Personally I like the potential of the strix embrace, but if you want a good example of abandoned fledglings just look to the demo for first edition Requiem, it had the characters turned and abandoned as part of an experiment in undirected development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:13:53-07:00","id":596668,"title":"","content":"The Ordo Dracul could well be behind such an Embrace.<br /> <br /> Also, it could be a crazy way to punish the sires: they could have been forced to Embrace and leave the childer, so they left assets the prince can use against them without any of the benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T07:49:18-07:00","id":596978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem#post595782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea about a group of anarchistic vampires trying to swell the ranks of unaligned vampires to undermine the Covenants through sheer numbers. But that still doesn't square to why they wouldn't stick around to tutor them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a plausible Carthian plot. Swell the ranks of the undead to put stress on the domain. The established powers would look down on such byblows, shutting them out of proper vampire society. This would make them easy pickings for Carthian recruiters who come back a year later to see who survived. Even if the youngsters are just killed out right by the powers-that-be, their deaths would symbolize the indifference of the establishment to the well-being of the average Kindred.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a member/pack of Belial's Brood would also work as the Sire(s). They would do it to sow chaos, as part of their Pursuit. <br /> <br /> Or a group of callous elders might to it as a test for their childer. Surviving a year as a newly made vampire, without any guidance or protection from your sire would be a brutally effective test of character/worth. In a Domain that strictly forbids the Embrace such a method would also be necessary to protect the status of the Elders in question, by concealing their identities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:51:03-07:00","id":597120,"title":"","content":"It's also a Masquerade Breach begging to happen. I'm not saying that isn't a good way to do it, but one should factor how they intend to deal with that into the plan, if there is one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:22:43-07:00","id":598432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem#post595782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm starting up a campaign which may include new players. As such I don't want to toss them into the deep end of vampric politics. So I have an idea for a less social and more personal campaign, but I'm trying to come up with a good initial justification for it. Essentially I want to have a group of players who are turned then dumped by the wayside without learning so much that sun bathing is a really bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently wrapped up a chronicle based on this idea, actually . . . The players created mortal characters using the WoD rules and I gave each of them a short prelude separately, but the one commonality was that they didn't remember anything about their Embrace; they all came to after the fact and had to figure it out for themselves, hunger, frenzy, sunlight, predatory aura, revenants, and all. Eventually they did run afoul of local Kindred, Gauru, Strix, and other things, and began finding their place in the food chain (while scrambling to learn about their condition, make themselves useful to other Kindred, and justify their existence to the Prince). They never found out who their sire(s) were, if any (wandering Kindred? Strix? Something else? Who knows?) . . . I left it a mystery.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point: it was a hellish, fun, dramatic ride. And your idea, I think, would be perfect for a game that's largely personal and emotional rather than political. Having no sire, and no previous connection to to supernatural, meant that each player/character had to rely on their own knowledge and what connections they could use from their previous lives, and each other (although their gradual entanglement into Kindred politics also further complicated things, as it does), and determine what their Requiem meant to them, and them alone, not because of their sire or other pre existing political connections.<br /> <br /> All the players were also new to WoD / VtR (and it sounds like yours are too?), so throwing them in like this actually helped with immersing them in a story that was largely personal, since neither they nor their characters hardly had any idea what was going on (aside from understanding the mechanics, of course) and were learning as they went along. I say do it, and good luck; it'll probably be good mad blood spattered fun! Don't be surprised if the early episodes feel like the Marx Brothers with fangs. It might be a hilarious, horrific comedy of errors, but they'll be (orphan?) neonates, so, par for the course!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 07-21-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:42:15-07:00","id":598529,"title":"","content":"Lucid: I strongly suggest checking out the vampire demo that was linked by Rose before. Adapt it to your preferred setting, but it does exactly what you're looking for, barring a couple of edition mechanic mismatches that you can see from a mile away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T14:56:15-07:00","id":602286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem?p=595930#post595930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the quieter motives behind putting revenants in the 2e core was to provide a way for groups to be Embraced. Your characters could have all been fed on by vampires, then &quot;died&quot; on the way home in a car accident or something. The revenant rules are a bit punishing to hit an entire coterie with at once, but you could just borrow the metaphysics and start the player characters as regular neonates.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full\" target=\"_blank\">first edition demo</a> also provides a justification for a diverse coterie of newly Embraced vampires, and in general works as a crash course in the setting for new characters and players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question wouldn't those be the other rise from the dead vamps? As full vamps?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:35:29-07:00","id":612564,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input everyone!<br /> <br /> I'm just going to have the players awaken in the hotel a night after Burning Man. I'm not going to put a lot of thought into how and why at the moment. I'm just going to focus on the personal aspect of their condition. I also decided that instead of there being no direction from their sires, that they are going to be lead around by a series of letters, phone calls, and obscure messages in order to test their mettle.<br /> <br /> I do sort of have an idea for an idea. I have the image in my head of an elder Nosferatu who claims to be an Ancient. He's disturbing even among Nosferatu standards. He has a massive hydrocephaliac head that looks like a fleshy malformed watermelon. Large oversized that are dark and clouded over. A nose that's withered back to a hole in his face and a tiny, understated jaw. A body like a malnourished toddler. Arms and legs like crooked chicken wings. All shoved into an elaborate wheelchair that caters to his needs. I'm envisioning what looks like a creepy gray alien/human hybrid gone wrong. <br /> <br /> He's an Ordo Dracul who seeks to overcome his very obvious issues as well as the curse of Malkavia. Is, or believes that he was once a member of the Knights Templar. Has, or believes that he is in possession of the Ark of the Covenant. Believes that exposure to the Ark over a long period of time is what's reduced him to this state. He fled a Lacena Sanctum controlled city who believed him to be a mad heretic. The Prince of the city didn't like that so many were buying his BS. So this still unnamed Nosferatu seeks revenge. So his biding his time and is building a force of hardy vampires who will be able to stand up to the &quot;soft&quot; kindred of the city.<br /> <br /> But all of this is on the back burner. I'm focusing on the players to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:11:18-07:00","id":612636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem?p=612564#post612564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the input everyone!<br /> <br /> I'm just going to have the players awaken in the hotel a night after Burning Man. I'm not going to put a lot of thought into how and why at the moment. I'm just going to focus on the personal aspect of their condition. I also decided that instead of there being no direction from their sires, that they are going to be lead around by a series of letters, phone calls, and obscure messages in order to test their mettle.<br /> <br /> I do sort of have an idea for an idea. I have the image in my head of an elder Nosferatu who claims to be an Ancient. He's disturbing even among Nosferatu standards. He has a massive hydrocephaliac head that looks like a fleshy malformed watermelon. Large oversized that are dark and clouded over. A nose that's withered back to a hole in his face and a tiny, understated jaw. A body like a malnourished toddler. Arms and legs like crooked chicken wings. All shoved into an elaborate wheelchair that caters to his needs. I'm envisioning what looks like a creepy gray alien/human hybrid gone wrong.<br /> <br /> He's an Ordo Dracul who seeks to overcome his very obvious issues as well as the curse of Malkavia. Is, or believes that he was once a member of the Knights Templar. Has, or believes that he is in possession of the Ark of the Covenant. Believes that exposure to the Ark over a long period of time is what's reduced him to this state. He fled a Lacena Sanctum controlled city who believed him to be a mad heretic. The Prince of the city didn't like that so many were buying his BS. So this still unnamed Nosferatu seeks revenge. So his biding his time and is building a force of hardy vampires who will be able to stand up to the &quot;soft&quot; kindred of the city.<br /> <br /> But all of this is on the back burner. I'm focusing on the players to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>See P. 93 of Blood and Smoke about posthumous embracing. As I read it They don't have to be revenants which are on P. 94.<br /> Also review the new rules for blood ties. That has all kinds of possibilities for foreshadowing and mystery in this case.<br /> Then look into rules for first tier play.<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tier\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tier<br /> <br /> It was either the chroniclers guide or Dance Macabre that dealt with this.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T23:23:46-07:00","id":625159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/595782-no-tutor-no-problem?p=612564#post612564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the image in my head of an elder Nosferatu . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole description sounds somewhere between Aphex Twin's &quot;Rubber Johnny&quot; and the vampire kid from the &quot;Meanwhile&quot; parts of Johnen Vasquez's JTHM comics.<br /> <br /> I like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}